  "content": {
    "_uid": "ad980c5b-1d12-f591-2806-5348f24f8dc6",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "649e6c25-4d8f-fb7a-43d4-3606a6f33367",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "30 participants including government officials, faculty from different institutions and master trainers from Balochistan attended the programme titled, 'Introduction to Early Childhood Education Curriculum' conducted in Karachi from February 23 to March 6, 2015. The programme provided the participants an opportunity to enhance their understanding of the National Curriculum for Early Childhood Education (2007) and effective implementation of pedagogical strategies in the early years setting.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Another CPE programme titled 'Formative Classroom Assessment', which was conducted in Quetta from March 16-28, 2015, brought together 47 teachers and teacher educators from different institutes in Balochistan. The programme focused on enhancing the course participants' understanding of formative and summative assessment; the basic principles and methods of classroom assessment; and designing basic assessment tools for their own classrooms.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The participants' from both programmes appreciated the content knowledge and expertise of the faculty and the practical relevance, which the course had for the enhancement of their current job skills.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
